  "title": "Publication of Silent Spring",
  "summary": "Silent Spring, Rachel Carson's book on chemical pesticides, especially DDT, and their threat to wildlife and human health, was published on 27 September 1962 after a New Yorker serialization. It sold more than 600,000 copies in its first year, is credited with helping launch the modern environmental movement, and a federal DDT ban followed in 1972.",
